# Pairs with AtomicOnOwner. Reproduces current production: a saga bound to the
# resized copy R whose resize is undone after the swap sends its terminals to R
# directly; R's armed redirect answers StaleTreeRoutingException, and
# MarkOneShardAsync refreshes routing and re-sends the shard's terminal, with
# its committed-values backstop, to the old copy, which the undo made the tree
# again and which lays keys out by the same map. Terminals R took before the
# undo are discarded with R, so the old copy gets the batch on some shards only.
MODULE: AtomicOnOwnerDiscardedCopyTerminalRedirects
TARGET: AtomicOnOwner
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: terminals of a saga bound to an undone resized copy are re-sent to the old copy, landing part of the batch there
PERTURBS: SagaTerminal

--- FIND
           hit == IF bound = R /\ ~Live(R) THEN {}
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: a terminal R's redirect refuses is re-sent to the old copy.
           hit == IF bound = R /\ ~Live(R) THEN {<<T, s>>}
--- END
